<title>UK: UK grain futures close lower on thin market.</title>
<headline>UK grain futures close lower on thin market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK grain futures closed lower on Monday on a thinly traded market.</p>
<p>&quot;People expected futures to drop a lot more than they have on currency,&quot; said a trader.</p>
<p>Wheat closed 0.15 to 0.55 stg down after trading 221 lots, while barley was 0.45 stg lower on 25 lots.</p>
<p>Cash trading was light with most players sidelined by the smaller than expected fall in the futures.</p>
<p>Amsterdam milling wheat futures were neglected.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
